  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1220 AM CST Wed Nov 18 2026\n\nGusty winds return Thursday afternoon/evening with gusts up to 15 to \n25 mph across the Permian Basin and higher elevations to the west. \nIn the upper levels, a more stable pattern returns to the area, \nbringing dry conditions through the remainder of the work week. This \nweek end, and upper-level shortwave trough is forecast to move north \nof our forecast area, but a cold front from the trough is expected \nto extend down across the region, bringing cooler temperatures \nbeginning around Saturday evening into Sunday morning. Rain chances \nfrom this system remain low (<10%) as the best moisture and \nstrongest lift will be to our east and north, respectively. Into \nearly next week, another, but deeper, shortwave trough is expected \nto move into the region, bringing stronger light and higher moisture \nlevels, thus increasing rain chances into early next week.\n\nBynum",
